\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.8}{\ignorespaces Architecture and data flow in the CMS Level-1 trigger system. The calorimeter trigger processes energy deposits from the ECAL, HCAL, and HF, while the muon trigger combines information from the DT, CSC, and RPC detectors. Both paths converge at the Global Trigger, which issues the L1 Accept decision within a latency of less than 3.2\nobreakspace {}$\mu $s\nobreakspace {}\blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {CMS:2020cmk}.\relax }}{49}{figure.caption.46}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.9}{\ignorespaces HLT output rates in CMS. Panel (a) shows total, shared, and pure HLT rates by physics category at $\mathcal {L} = 2.0 \times 10^{34}\ensuremath {\,\text {cm}^\text {$-$2}\,\text {s}^\text {$-$1}}\xspace $ during 2018 data-taking\nobreakspace {}\blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {CMS:2024aqx}. Panel (b) shows HLT stream rates during a typical Run\nobreakspace {}3 fill (Fill\nobreakspace {}10690, June 2025), showing the Standard, Parking, Scouting, Calibration/Monitoring, and Express streams together with the delivered luminosity and L1T rate\nobreakspace {}\blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {CMS-DP-2025-034}.\relax }}{50}{figure.caption.47}%
